sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch06-08> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Two-dimensional cellular automata exhibit the same four classes of behavior as one-dimensional ones, which becomes evident when one-dimensional slices through their evolution are examined; class 4 behavior, as in the Game of Life, occurs even on a white background with slightly more complicated rules.";
    dc:type "computational-observation";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Two-dimensional cellular automata show the same four classes";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 6, “Starting from Randomness”; section “Four Classes of Behavior” (from p. 231), p. 245. Scope: two-dimensional cellular automata"
}
